00:32:20.529 --> 00:32:23.279
minutes, and then my wife yelled, pancakes are ready and my

00:32:23.279 --> 00:32:26.429
younger daughter was like, dad was really weird. And so I

00:32:26.449 --> 00:32:31.269
wonder where is there a point on the web, is it, if you add

00:32:31.289 --> 00:32:34.199
location into it, if you all the other data you are putting

00:32:34.199 --> 00:32:37.199
in like what you are watching on Netflix or what you are

00:32:37.199 --> 00:32:39.970
buying at Wal-Mart or whatever it may be, where

00:32:39.990 --> 00:32:44.279
personalization has gotten to the point where you are just

00:32:44.299 --> 00:32:47.299
like, that's weird, like they know too much about me, and I

00:32:47.299 --> 00:32:50.299
am curious how you guys feel about that, is that coming or

00:32:50.299 --> 00:32:52.549
are we there or what does that look like.

00:32:52.549 --> 00:32:56.449
Let me start by saying that there is an interesting product

00:32:56.469 --> 00:33:01.639
there, which is on your mobile phone to implicitly infer

00:33:01.659 --> 00:33:04.669
your interest at the moment and then broadcast it to your

00:33:04.689 --> 00:33:10.069
friends and so your app fix that you are going to like

00:33:10.089 --> 00:33:14.460
pancakes, it will tell your parents. In terms of weird, I

00:33:14.480 --> 00:33:18.759
think we will progressively be more weird, I think that what

00:33:18.779 --> 00:33:22.139
we think is weird now will become normal.

00:33:22.159 --> 00:33:24.659
I mean weird like some people might consider that privacy

00:33:24.659 --> 00:33:26.169
was inundated or what is privacy --.

00:33:26.189 --> 00:33:28.689
Yeah I think cultural norms and privacy, I have definitely

00:33:28.689 --> 00:33:32.839
changed dramatically over last ten years, and will continue

00:33:32.859 --> 00:33:38.349
to change, in ways that will surprise us when we have kids

00:33:38.369 --> 00:33:43.299
and so mean there is a real change and there is a real

00:33:43.319 --> 00:33:46.449
intergenerational change in terms of perception of privacy.

00:33:46.469 --> 00:33:51.710
And I think to add to that, you mentioned when people were

00:33:51.730 --> 00:33:54.230
scared of putting their credit card numbers online and I

00:33:54.230 --> 00:33:56.730
remember when I started at Myspace, people were scared of

00:33:56.730 --> 00:33:59.230
putting a photo online or putting their real name online.

00:33:59.230 --> 00:34:00.980
And I was scared, I don't know

00:34:00.980 --> 00:34:05.960
[inaudible] do this. But once I did, I started to value in

00:34:05.980 --> 00:34:09.880
it. And so I think you know the sort of stage that we are

00:34:09.900 --> 00:34:12.889
out with personalization is somewhat similar where, what is

00:34:12.909 --> 00:34:16.029
happening right now is there is a fear in the unknown, like

00:34:16.049 --> 00:34:20.440
right now we project these potential disaster scenarios

00:34:20.460 --> 00:34:23.250
because we don't know what's going to happen. And so I think

00:34:23.250 --> 00:34:26.170
what will more logically end up happening is what you have

00:34:26.190 --> 00:34:29.139
to do is first educate the user, as to what's happening. You

00:34:29.139 --> 00:34:31.799
show them value for what's happening as a result of that.

00:34:31.799 --> 00:34:35.469
You build trust in your relationship with them. And then

00:34:35.489 --> 00:34:38.239
they are going to be a little bit more forthcoming with

00:34:38.239 --> 00:34:41.829
their data. I don't know if or when we will get to a place

00:34:41.829 --> 00:34:43.829
where everything is completely transparent, I can't imagine

00:34:43.829 --> 00:34:46.829
that being the case. So I think that we will have certain

00:34:46.829 --> 00:34:49.079
things about us, if it's health related maybe financially

00:34:49.079 --> 00:34:53.319
related, maybe not or kept a little bit more secure, a

00:34:53.339 --> 00:34:57.389
little bit more private. But I think that like every sort of

00:34:57.409 --> 00:35:00.190
disruptive technology will deal with those hurdles as they

00:35:00.210 --> 00:35:03.889
come and we will figure out the right way to react to them.

00:35:03.909 --> 00:35:08.599
But I think that by far the value that we will get out of it

00:35:08.619 --> 00:35:11.579
very much outweighs the risks that we are taking. So it's

00:35:11.579 --> 00:35:14.389
very much in our interest to push those boundaries and just

00:35:14.409 --> 00:35:17.190
try to figure out where that equilibrium is.

